{
"answer": "Overfitting occurs when a machine learning model learns the training data too well, capturing noise and random fluctuations rather than the underlying pattern, which leads to poor generalization on unseen data. Two common ways to prevent it are regularization (such as L1 or L2) and cross-validation.",
"confidence": "high",
"key_points": [
"Model learns training data noise instead of general patterns",
"Results in poor performance on unseen data",
"Prevented using regularization techniques like L1/L2",
"Prevented using techniques like cross-validation and dropout"
]
}

